<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Westerwald</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Westerwald is a low mountain range east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> between the Sieg, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lahn">Lahn</a> and Dill rivers, mainly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhineland-palatinate">Rhineland-Palatinate</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was divided among the counts of Sayn, Nassau, Isenburg and Wied. The area is known for its salt-glazed stoneware, made in the district called the Kannenbäckerland, and for basalt quarrying.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/westerwald.jpg" alt="Westerwald" width="320" height="221" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Oliver Abels (SBT) · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arborn_Panorama.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
